{"module":"many-targets","voice":"female","duration":300.8,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Muchos blancos: comunidades latinas, asiáticas, indígenas e inmigrantes","start":0.0,"end":5.75,"words":[[0.06,0.51],[0.51,1.12],[1.38,2.21],[2.21,2.81],[3.08,3.83],[4.09,4.77],[4.77,4.85],[4.85,5.68]]},{"el":"intro","text":"La misma maquinaria de leyes, turbas y acusaciones falsas se ha dirigido contra muchas comunidades.","start":6.55,"end":12.89,"words":[[6.67,6.8],[6.8,7.14],[7.14,7.75],[7.75,7.88],[7.88,8.29],[8.52,8.93],[8.93,9.0],[9.0,9.74],[9.74,10.14],[10.14,10.28],[10.28,10.35],[10.35,10.89],[10.89,11.29],[11.29,11.7],[11.7,12.51]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Ver el panorama completo construye coaliciones, y las coaliciones aprueban leyes.","start":13.24,"end":18.6,"words":[[13.34,13.53],[13.53,13.66],[13.66,14.19],[14.19,14.71],[14.71,15.3],[15.3,16.09],[16.32,16.38],[16.38,16.58],[16.58,17.3],[17.3,17.82],[17.82,18.22]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Mexicoamericanos","start":18.95,"end":20.33,"words":[[19.06,20.27]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Los historiadores William Carrigan y Clive Webb documentaron al menos 547 linchamientos de mexicanos en Estados Unidos entre 1848 y 1928.","start":21.03,"end":33.19,"words":[[21.14,21.33],[21.33,22.11],[22.11,22.63],[22.63,23.08],[23.08,23.14],[23.14,23.46],[23.46,23.72],[23.72,24.5],[24.5,24.63],[24.63,24.95],[24.95,26.43],[26.43,27.27],[27.27,27.4],[27.4,27.98],[27.98,28.11],[28.11,28.56],[28.56,28.95],[28.95,29.27],[29.27,31.08],[31.08,31.14],[31.14,32.82]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En enero de 1918, Rangers de Texas, soldados y rancheros locales mataron a 15 hombres y niños mexicanos en Porvenir, Texas.","start":33.54,"end":43.8,"words":[[33.64,33.78],[33.78,34.13],[34.13,34.28],[34.28,36.05],[36.3,36.8],[36.8,36.94],[36.94,37.44],[37.69,38.26],[38.26,38.33],[38.33,38.97],[38.97,39.46],[39.46,39.96],[39.96,40.03],[40.03,40.39],[40.39,40.81],[40.81,40.89],[40.89,41.24],[41.24,41.88],[41.88,42.02],[42.02,42.66],[42.91,43.41]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En Mendez v. Westminster (1947), familias mexicoamericanas ganaron un caso contra la segregación escolar en California, siete años antes de Brown v. Board.","start":44.15,"end":56.19,"words":[[44.24,44.37],[44.37,44.77],[44.77,44.97],[45.3,46.03],[46.03,47.95],[48.19,48.72],[48.72,49.78],[49.78,50.24],[50.24,50.38],[50.38,50.64],[50.64,51.04],[51.04,51.17],[51.17,51.9],[51.9,52.37],[52.37,52.5],[52.5,53.23],[53.46,53.79],[53.79,54.06],[54.06,54.39],[54.39,54.52],[54.52,54.85],[54.85,55.05],[55.38,55.78]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1943, militares atacaron a jóvenes mexicoamericanos en Los Ángeles en los “disturbios de los Zoot Suit”, y la policía arrestó a las víctimas.","start":56.54,"end":66.91,"words":[[56.62,56.75],[56.75,58.61],[58.85,59.44],[59.44,59.98],[59.98,60.04],[60.04,60.51],[60.51,61.57],[61.57,61.7],[61.7,61.9],[61.9,62.37],[62.37,62.5],[62.5,62.7],[62.7,63.37],[63.37,63.5],[63.5,63.7],[63.7,63.96],[63.96,64.3],[64.53,64.6],[64.6,64.73],[64.73,65.26],[65.26,65.66],[65.66,65.73],[65.73,65.93],[65.93,66.52]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 2019, un hombre armado que había publicado sobre una “invasión hispana” mató a 23 personas en un Walmart de El Paso.","start":67.26,"end":76.41,"words":[[67.33,67.48],[67.48,68.74],[69.0,69.15],[69.15,69.52],[69.52,69.97],[69.97,70.11],[70.11,70.49],[70.49,71.15],[71.15,71.53],[71.53,71.75],[71.75,72.34],[72.34,72.79],[72.79,73.09],[73.09,73.16],[73.16,73.9],[73.9,74.5],[74.5,74.65],[74.65,74.8],[74.8,75.32],[75.32,75.47],[75.47,75.61],[75.61,75.99]]},{"el":"s0","text":"(Ver también el módulo sobre las fronteras.)","start":76.76,"end":79.33,"words":[[76.83,77.01],[77.01,77.45],[77.45,77.58],[77.58,77.95],[77.95,78.27],[78.27,78.45],[78.45,79.08]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Asiático-americanos","start":80.23,"end":81.74,"words":[[80.32,81.68]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Inmigrantes chinos fueron masacrados en Los Ángeles (1871) y Rock Springs (1885) y expulsados de Tacoma (1885).","start":82.44,"end":94.4,"words":[[82.49,83.27],[83.27,83.69],[83.69,84.12],[84.12,84.82],[84.82,84.96],[84.96,85.17],[85.17,85.67],[85.67,87.5],[87.75,87.82],[87.82,88.03],[88.03,88.45],[88.45,90.36],[90.61,90.68],[90.68,91.45],[91.45,91.59],[91.59,92.02],[92.02,93.99]]},{"el":"s1","text":"La Ley de Exclusión China (1882) fue la primera ley de EE. UU. que prohibió la entrada de un grupo por su nacionalidad.","start":94.75,"end":103.27,"words":[[94.86,94.99],[94.99,95.17],[95.17,95.3],[95.3,95.93],[95.93,96.24],[96.24,97.8],[98.02,98.21],[98.21,98.34],[98.34,98.78],[98.78,98.96],[98.96,99.09],[99.09,99.28],[99.59,99.78],[100.09,100.22],[100.22,100.65],[100.65,100.78],[100.78,101.22],[101.22,101.34],[101.34,101.47],[101.47,101.78],[101.78,101.97],[101.97,102.09],[102.09,102.91]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Unos 120,000 japoneses-estadounidenses, la mayoría ciudadanos, fueron encarcelados durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial.","start":103.62,"end":112.96,"words":[[103.73,104.0],[104.0,105.89],[105.89,107.58],[107.81,107.95],[107.95,108.49],[108.49,109.23],[109.46,109.87],[109.87,110.68],[110.68,111.15],[111.15,111.28],[111.28,111.76],[111.76,112.03],[112.03,112.56]]},{"el":"s1","text":"En 1982, Vincent Chin fue golpeado hasta la muerte en Detroit por dos trabajadores automotrices blancos que culpaban a Japón de la pérdida de empleos; fueron condenados a libertad condicional y a una multa de $3,000, lo que desató un movimiento nacional por los derechos civiles asiático-americanos.","start":113.31,"end":135.88,"words":[[113.39,113.53],[113.53,115.45],[115.71,116.22],[116.22,116.52],[116.52,116.74],[116.74,117.33],[117.33,117.62],[117.62,117.77],[117.77,118.21],[118.21,118.36],[118.36,118.88],[118.88,119.1],[119.1,119.32],[119.32,120.2],[120.2,121.09],[121.09,121.6],[121.6,121.75],[121.75,122.34],[122.34,122.41],[122.41,122.78],[122.78,122.93],[122.93,123.08],[123.08,123.59],[123.59,123.74],[123.74,124.33],[124.59,125.03],[125.03,125.77],[125.77,125.84],[125.84,126.43],[126.43,127.24],[127.24,127.31],[127.31,127.39],[127.39,127.61],[127.61,127.98],[127.98,128.13],[128.13,130.04],[130.3,130.45],[130.45,130.59],[130.59,131.04],[131.04,131.18],[131.18,131.92],[131.92,132.51],[132.51,132.73],[132.73,132.95],[132.95,133.54],[133.54,134.06],[134.06,135.46]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Después del 11 de septiembre, sijs y estadounidenses del sur de Asia fueron atacados, empezando por el asesinato de Balbir Singh Sodhi en Arizona pocos días después.","start":136.23,"end":147.2,"words":[[136.33,136.82],[136.82,137.03],[137.03,137.31],[137.31,137.45],[137.45,138.23],[138.48,138.76],[138.76,138.83],[138.83,139.88],[139.88,140.09],[140.09,140.31],[140.31,140.45],[140.45,140.73],[140.73,141.15],[141.15,141.79],[142.03,142.67],[142.67,142.88],[142.88,143.02],[143.02,143.65],[143.65,143.79],[143.79,144.22],[144.22,144.5],[144.5,144.78],[144.78,144.92],[144.92,145.41],[145.41,145.76],[145.76,146.12],[146.12,146.68]]},{"el":"s1","text":"De 2020 a 2021, Stop AAPI Hate recibió más de 10,000 reportes de incidentes de odio antiasiático, y en marzo de 2021 un hombre armado mató a ocho personas, seis de ellas mujeres asiáticas, en spas del área de Atlanta.","start":147.55,"end":165.13,"words":[[147.64,147.78],[147.78,148.65],[148.65,148.72],[148.72,149.95],[150.2,150.49],[150.49,150.78],[150.78,151.0],[151.0,151.51],[151.51,151.72],[151.72,151.87],[151.87,153.31],[153.31,153.89],[153.89,154.04],[154.04,154.76],[154.76,154.9],[154.9,155.19],[155.19,156.13],[156.38,156.46],[156.46,156.6],[156.6,156.96],[156.96,157.11],[157.11,158.26],[158.26,158.41],[158.41,158.77],[158.77,159.2],[159.2,159.49],[159.49,159.57],[159.57,159.85],[159.85,160.5],[160.76,161.05],[161.05,161.19],[161.19,161.55],[161.55,162.06],[162.06,162.78],[163.03,163.18],[163.18,163.47],[163.47,163.69],[163.69,163.97],[163.97,164.12],[164.12,164.7]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Pueblos indígenas","start":166.03,"end":167.4,"words":[[166.13,166.65],[166.65,167.33]]},{"el":"s2","text":"No todos los indígenas recibieron la ciudadanía estadounidense hasta 1924, y Arizona y Nuevo México les prohibieron votar hasta 1948.","start":168.1,"end":179.21,"words":[[168.18,168.31],[168.31,168.64],[168.64,168.84],[168.84,169.43],[169.43,170.09],[170.09,170.22],[170.22,170.95],[170.95,171.87],[171.87,172.14],[172.14,173.92],[174.15,174.22],[174.22,174.68],[174.68,174.75],[174.75,175.08],[175.08,175.47],[175.47,175.67],[175.67,176.33],[176.33,176.66],[176.66,176.93],[176.93,178.84]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los internados federales se tratan en el módulo sobre la conquista.","start":179.56,"end":183.41,"words":[[179.64,179.82],[179.82,180.43],[180.43,180.98],[180.98,181.1],[181.1,181.47],[181.47,181.59],[181.59,181.72],[181.72,182.08],[182.08,182.39],[182.39,182.51],[182.51,183.06]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Hoy, las mujeres indígenas americanas y nativas de Alaska enfrentan tasas muy altas de violencia.","start":183.76,"end":190.08,"words":[[183.81,184.02],[184.26,184.46],[184.46,184.94],[184.94,185.56],[185.56,186.25],[186.25,186.32],[186.32,186.8],[186.8,186.94],[186.94,187.35],[187.35,187.97],[187.97,188.31],[188.31,188.52],[188.52,188.86],[188.86,189.0],[189.0,189.68]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Un informe de 2018 del Urban Indian Health Institute señaló que, de 5,712 casos de mujeres y niñas indígenas desaparecidas reportados a la base de datos del FBI en 2016, solo 116 figuraban en la base de datos federal de personas desaparecidas.","start":190.43,"end":209.9,"words":[[190.53,190.67],[190.67,191.18],[191.18,191.32],[191.32,192.47],[192.47,192.69],[192.69,193.05],[193.05,193.48],[193.48,193.77],[193.77,194.42],[194.42,194.85],[194.85,195.07],[195.32,195.46],[195.46,197.19],[197.19,197.55],[197.55,197.7],[197.7,198.2],[198.2,198.27],[198.27,198.64],[198.64,199.28],[199.28,200.22],[200.22,200.94],[200.94,201.01],[201.01,201.16],[201.16,201.45],[201.45,201.59],[201.59,201.95],[201.95,202.17],[202.17,202.6],[202.6,202.74],[202.74,203.9],[204.15,204.44],[204.44,205.52],[205.52,206.17],[206.17,206.31],[206.31,206.46],[206.46,206.74],[206.74,206.89],[206.89,207.25],[207.25,207.75],[207.75,207.9],[207.9,208.47],[208.47,209.48]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En 2020, el Congreso aprobó la Ley Savanna y la Ley Not Invisible para mejorar el seguimiento y la investigación de estos casos.","start":210.25,"end":219.56,"words":[[210.33,210.48],[210.48,211.46],[211.72,211.88],[211.88,212.48],[212.48,212.93],[212.93,213.08],[213.08,213.31],[213.31,213.84],[213.84,213.92],[213.92,214.07],[214.07,214.29],[214.29,214.52],[214.52,215.2],[215.2,215.5],[215.5,216.03],[216.03,216.18],[216.18,216.94],[216.94,217.01],[217.01,217.16],[217.16,218.15],[218.15,218.3],[218.3,218.67],[218.67,219.13]]},{"el":"h3","text":"La violencia policial en distintos grupos","start":220.46,"end":223.14,"words":[[220.53,220.67],[220.67,221.3],[221.3,221.87],[221.87,222.01],[222.01,222.64],[222.64,223.06]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Algunos análisis de las muertes a manos de la policía, ajustados por población, sitúan a los indígenas americanos en el primer lugar o cerca, seguidos por los estadounidenses negros; otros los ordenan distinto.","start":223.84,"end":237.63,"words":[[223.92,224.4],[224.4,224.96],[224.96,225.1],[225.1,225.3],[225.3,225.79],[225.79,225.86],[225.86,226.2],[226.2,226.34],[226.34,226.48],[226.48,227.1],[227.35,227.97],[227.97,228.18],[228.18,228.87],[229.11,229.53],[229.53,229.6],[229.6,229.8],[229.8,230.43],[230.43,231.12],[231.12,231.26],[231.26,231.4],[231.4,231.81],[231.81,232.16],[232.16,232.23],[232.23,232.64],[232.89,233.37],[233.37,233.58],[233.58,233.79],[233.79,234.82],[234.82,235.31],[235.55,235.9],[235.9,236.11],[236.11,236.59],[236.59,237.21]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Las cifras son inciertas porque la raza de las víctimas indígenas y latinas a menudo se registra mal.","start":237.98,"end":244.19,"words":[[238.11,238.32],[238.32,238.73],[238.73,238.93],[238.93,239.55],[239.55,239.89],[239.89,240.03],[240.03,240.3],[240.3,240.44],[240.44,240.65],[240.65,241.19],[241.19,241.81],[241.81,241.88],[241.88,242.36],[242.36,242.43],[242.43,242.84],[242.84,242.97],[242.97,243.52],[243.52,243.8]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La capa de muertes a manos de la policía del mapa (Mapping Police Violence) colorea cada caso según la raza de la víctima para que veas el patrón por tu cuenta.","start":244.54,"end":253.76,"words":[[244.66,244.8],[244.8,245.06],[245.06,245.2],[245.2,245.66],[245.66,245.73],[245.73,246.06],[246.06,246.19],[246.19,246.33],[246.33,246.86],[246.86,247.06],[247.06,247.33],[247.33,247.73],[247.73,248.13],[248.13,248.66],[248.89,249.36],[249.36,249.62],[249.62,249.89],[249.89,250.22],[250.22,250.36],[250.36,250.62],[250.62,250.75],[250.75,250.89],[250.89,251.35],[251.35,251.62],[251.62,251.75],[251.75,252.02],[252.02,252.15],[252.15,252.55],[252.55,252.75],[252.75,252.88],[252.88,253.35]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Unidos","start":254.66,"end":255.34,"words":[[254.73,255.29]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Frederick Douglass habló contra la exclusión china en su discurso “Nación compuesta” de 1869.","start":256.04,"end":262.76,"words":[[256.12,256.62],[256.62,257.12],[257.12,257.37],[257.37,257.75],[257.75,257.87],[257.87,258.5],[258.5,258.81],[258.81,258.94],[258.94,259.06],[259.06,259.56],[259.56,259.94],[259.94,260.51],[260.51,260.63],[260.63,262.39]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En 1965, trabajadores agrícolas filipinos encabezados por Larry Itliong iniciaron la huelga de la uva de Delano y pidieron al sindicato mexicoamericano de César Chávez que se uniera; juntos lograron los primeros grandes contratos para trabajadores agrícolas.","start":263.11,"end":281.07,"words":[[263.19,263.33],[263.33,265.29],[265.54,266.38],[266.38,267.01],[267.01,267.65],[267.65,268.42],[268.42,268.63],[268.63,268.91],[268.91,269.4],[269.4,270.03],[270.03,270.17],[270.17,270.52],[270.52,270.66],[270.66,270.8],[270.8,271.01],[271.01,271.15],[271.15,271.58],[271.58,271.65],[271.65,272.21],[272.21,272.35],[272.35,272.98],[272.98,274.03],[274.03,274.17],[274.17,274.52],[274.52,274.95],[274.95,275.09],[275.09,275.23],[275.23,275.72],[275.96,276.38],[276.38,276.95],[276.95,277.16],[277.16,277.72],[277.72,278.21],[278.21,278.84],[278.84,279.12],[279.12,279.96],[279.96,280.67]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La activista japonesa-estadounidense Yuri Kochiyama trabajó junto a Malcolm X y estaba con él cuando lo mataron.","start":281.42,"end":288.41,"words":[[281.51,281.64],[281.64,282.24],[282.24,283.69],[283.69,283.96],[283.96,284.56],[284.56,285.02],[285.02,285.35],[285.35,285.42],[285.42,285.88],[285.88,286.15],[286.15,286.21],[286.21,286.61],[286.61,286.81],[286.81,286.94],[286.94,287.34],[287.34,287.47],[287.47,288.0]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Organizadores negros, latinos, asiáticos e indígenas trabajaron juntos en las décadas de 1960 y 1970, y la Ley CAREN los protege a todos.","start":288.76,"end":299.95,"words":[[288.85,289.71],[289.71,290.18],[290.41,290.95],[291.18,291.78],[291.78,291.84],[291.84,292.44],[292.44,293.11],[293.11,293.51],[293.51,293.64],[293.64,293.84],[293.84,294.31],[294.31,294.44],[294.44,295.84],[295.84,295.91],[295.91,297.37],[297.61,297.67],[297.67,297.8],[297.8,298.0],[298.0,298.34],[298.34,298.54],[298.54,299.0],[299.0,299.07],[299.07,299.47]]}],"audio":"https://carenactmedia.blob.core.windows.net/audio/es/many-targets.female.58aa3b5f1c.mp3","bytes":1203618,"sha256":"58aa3b5f1c582add1b205e7f7adbf7ba294154c0c478c0bcaa41b99a6de01b28"}